// TEST: Antisymm pin on a named function through the eta wrapper
// A named function in kernel position is eta-expanded into a synthesized
// wrapper lambda built with NO where-clause, so every clause attribute needs
// its own surfacing side-channel or it is silently dropped (the wrapper then
// compiles a DENSE nest with no diagnostic — the long-standing `omp` bug).
// This is the anticomm twin of that surfacing: `where anticomm(a, b)` on the
// declaration must reach the wrapper and pin the same strict simplex the
// inline lambda gets in symmetry/020.
function diff(a, b) where anticomm(a, b) = a - b
let A = [1.0, 2.0, 3.0, 4.0]
let result = object_for(diff) <@> (A, A) |> compute
// Same six strict-triangle cells as symmetry/020 (A[i] - A[j], i < j).
// EXPECT: result = [-1.0, -2.0, -3.0, -1.0, -2.0, -1.0]
